            1. How to Seal Stamped Concrete: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Clean the slab, let the stamped texture dry completely, and apply two thin coats of a clear or tinted acrylic sealer with a sprayer and a back-roller, putting an anti-slip additive in the second coat. Most of the work is the prep and the waiting. The application itself takes a couple of hours on a typical 300 to 500 square foot patio, and the eight steps below are the whole job in order.
          </p>

