        <div id="best-sealant" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. What Is the Best Sealant for Stamped Concrete, Acrylic or Penetrating?
          </h2>

          <p>
            For most stamped patios the best sealant is a film-forming acrylic, because stamped concrete is a colored finish, not just a slab. The color hardener, integral pigment and the darker antiquing release that sits in the lows are thin surface layers. An acrylic film locks them in, deepens them to the &ldquo;just hosed down&rdquo; look most owners expect, and protects the release from wearing away under feet. That is why acrylic is the default in decorative-concrete trade guidance and why it tops our <a href="/best-stamped-concrete-sealer/">stamped concrete sealer</a> rankings.
          </p>

          <p>
            Acrylics come in two carriers. Solvent-based acrylics give the strongest color boost and, critically, re-dissolve when fresh sealer or solvent touches them, so new coats fuse with old ones and cloudy patches can often be cleared without stripping. Water-based acrylics smell far less and are sold where VOC rules are strict, but usually darken a little less and do not re-melt the same way.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
